{"meta":{"ph":"sniːz; NAmE sniːz","pos":"verb","stars":"★★"},"defs":[{"def":"to have air come suddenly and noisily out through your nose and mouth in a way that you cannot control, for example because you have a cold 打喷嚏noun","ex":[{"s":"This allows it to take in air at 30 times the speed of a human sneeze, enabling it to drink 3L of water a second.","src":"2022天津4月卷·阅读理解C","cat":"gaokao","year":2022,"t":"这使它能以人类打喷嚏30倍的速度吸入空气，从而每秒喝下3升水。"},{"s":"It lets out 64% more air when sneezing.","src":"2022天津4月卷·阅读理解C","cat":"gaokao","year":2022,"t":"它打喷嚏时多释放64%的空气。"},{"s":"Carrying out these everyday tasks effectively helps the astronauts stay healthy and focus on their work in space – after all, imagine what would happen if they caught a cold and started to sneeze!","src":"外研社B7 U6","cat":"waiyan","t":"执行这些日常任务有效地帮助宇航员保持健康,并专注于在太空的工作——毕竟,想象一下如果他们感冒并开始打喷嚏会发生什么事!"},{"s":"It affects the 2 and is passed on through tiny drops of saliva released when someone coughs or sneezes.","src":"北师大选必3 U9","cat":"beishida","t":"它影响2,通过微小滴唾液传递,当有人咳嗽或打喷嚏时释放出来."}]}]}